{# A real label, always. Never a placeholder standing in for one ([25.7]):
   a placeholder disappears on focus, which is exactly when it is needed.

   Left-aligned and small. These partials were transcribed from a mockup that
   put one question on a screen of its own, where a centered 28px label is the
   page; rendered two-up in a grid, as the form actually renders, every label
   competed with every other and with the page heading, and a five-field page
   read as five headlines. A label in a form names its box and gets out of the
   way -- the eye should land on the question text, then the input directly
   under it, which is what the shared left edge buys. #}
<label for="intake-{{ field.name }}" id="intake-{{ field.name }}-label" class="block text-sm font-semibold leading-snug text-heading">
  {{ field.label }}{% if field.required %}<span class="text-danger" aria-hidden="true"> *</span>{% endif %}
</label>
{% if field.description %}
  <p class="mt-1 text-sm leading-relaxed text-muted">{{ field.description }}</p>
{% endif %}
